// Diagnostic-quality fixture (CLAUDE.md §8). ONE syntax mistake: the `+` has no right
// operand. Asserted on by the `diagnoise-*` blocks in scripts/regression_repros.sh:
//   * the build must be REJECTED (no exe), and
//   * it must produce exactly ONE per-site error, with no parser internals
//     (`tokens[...]` kind dumps, the Pratt term `nud`) in the text.
// Before panic-mode recovery this 3-line program printed 2 errors; the sibling shape
// `let v = [1, 2, 3` printed 8 errors plus 43 raw token-dump lines.
fn main() -> i32:
  let x: i64 = 1 +
  return 42
